WEBVTT

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:06.100
Long time, no see...

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:08.380
But not really, I guess.

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:12.200
I can't believe you came 
without being asked to.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.120
It must be really important.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.490
It's no big deal.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:21.340
I just released one of my employees.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:57.600
The master is free to hire whomever he wishes.

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:59.590
<b>Mystery 12 "The Separation"</b>

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.510
And he's free to fire whomever he wants, too.

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:04.010
You were upset before when I didn't tell you

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:05.690
that I had hired someone.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:09.530
So I thought I should at least let you know.

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:11.880
Let me know, huh?

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:14.750
Oh?

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:15.280
What?

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:18.000
I was just wondering

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.030
if you've always been so conscientious.

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:24.540
Sorry to have bothered you, Legislator.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:27.680
As long as you're here,

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:31.290
can't you at least tell 
me why you let him go?

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:39.300
Ashiya-kun lost his ability to see yokai?

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:40.930
Yeah.

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:42.030
That's all?

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:43.920
That's reason enough.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.900
He can't see yokai anymore.

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:48.090
He's of no more use to the Mononokean.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:50.310
What other reason do I need?

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:52.330
As far as I can tell,

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:56.090
he only temporarily granted 
his sight to a yokai.

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:59.070
It's not like he'll never 
be able to see them again.

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:03.530
It was only supposed to last a 
few days, but it's been a week.

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:06.920
I don't have time to waste 
on useless employees.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.580
He'd just get in the way of my work.

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:13.830
"I'm not firing him unless you 
make a rule forcing me to."

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:17.680
Who's the person who said that to me?

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:18.890
The situation has—

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:21.790
Itsuki, do you regret it?

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:22.840
Huh?

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:25.350
Hiring him.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:30.200
This is a good opportunity.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.220
Isn't that what you think?

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:39.240
He's too emotionally invested in yokai.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:42.810
More than the job demands.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:45.130
For the same reason, I've caused 
plenty of trouble for—

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:49.530
So it's best for him if he 
remains unable to see them?

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:54.920
I understand why you're comparing 
Ashiya-kun to yourself.

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:58.150
You don't want him to experience 
what you've gone through.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:04.760
I had no idea you cared for him so much.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:07.800
You're being annoying.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.080
An employer is free to let his employees go,

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:14.400
but doesn't an employee 
also have a right to stay?

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:15.900
Huh?

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:22.320
Besides, did he really accept 
your decision that easily?

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:25.320
Whether he accepts it or not doesn't matter.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:26.410
I'm the master.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:30.410
Now that you mention it, how many 
people are in Ashiya-kun's family?

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:33.640
Huh? He said his mother runs a flower shop,

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:36.920
and he has an older sister who drinks 
all the time and comes home late.

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:38.190
What about his father?

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:40.170
He didn't mention him.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:42.410
Where is this coming from?

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:46.010
I just found it a bit interesting 
that he's a human named Ashiya

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:48.000
who can see yokai.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.930
Isn't that why you hired him, too?

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:53.660
So why don't you wait a little—

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.000
I'll get rid of anyone

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:58.570
who hinders my ability to exorcise yokai.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.550
As the master of the Mononokean.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:11.920
Hello?

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:12.920
Brother!

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:14.360
Oh, Shizuku.

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:16.430
Are you coming home early today?

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:18.120
This isn't the time for that!

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:19.640
Is Itsuki still there?

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:22.550
Yeah, he's still here.

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:32.120
<i>He didn't come today, either.</i>

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:34.140
<i>Maybe he's dealing with a difficult job.</i>

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:36.740
<i>One that involves a fiendish yokai.</i>

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:40.040
What's your deal?

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:41.320
Nothing.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:43.400
Ashiyan, did you bring your camera?

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:46.200
Yeah. Just one we had lying 
around at home, though.

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:47.980
That's good enough.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:49.950
You're really joining the photography club?

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:52.380
I haven't decided yet.

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:53.150
Oh, okay.

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:53.950
Yeah.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:09.820
That's nice.

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:11.870
Ashiyan, you might have a knack for this.

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:13.580
You think so?

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:16.920
You've got a good sense for framing.

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:21.780
You should try taking some 
pictures on the way home, too.

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:27.400
<i>I'd only ever taken souvenir photos before.</i>

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.780
<i>Photography is more fun than I thought.</i>

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:32.120
<i>It'd be even better if I could 
take pictures of yokai...</i>

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:53.080
Zenko?

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:56.010
So you really did join the photography club.

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:58.410
I'm just a trial member for now,

00:06:58.410 --> 00:07:00.430
but it's pretty fun once you give it a shot.

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:02.100
Did you quit your job?

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:05.350
I didn't exactly quit.

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:07.840
I was fired.

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:09.650
Because you can't see yokai anymore?

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:10.780
Huh?

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:15.180
I see. Yahiko told you.

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:17.660
Yeah, and I thought of something.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.400
Thought of what?

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:21.370
I couldn't see them,

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:23.670
but I could after Yahiko bit me.

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:27.420
I thought you might get your 
sight back if Yahiko bit you.

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:30.880
That's it! We can try that!

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:33.140
Let's go see Yahiko right away!

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:41.840
I'm home.

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:44.190
<i>Is it okay for me to come over this late?</i>

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:47.270
<i>And, if I'm coming home with Zenko, her dad...</i>

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:50.440
Zenko, you're awfully late today.

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:52.350
<i>He was already waiting for us?!</i>

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:53.400
You.

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:55.620
Sorry! I have a good reas—

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:57.050
I'm glad you're here.

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:57.320
Huh?

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:58.690
Come in, come in.

00:07:58.690 --> 00:07:59.480
Whoa, wha—

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:08.140
Um, I'm sorry for dropping in so late.

00:08:08.140 --> 00:08:11.680
I was just thinking about asking 
Zenko to invite you over.

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:13.130
Huh? Me?

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:18.140
I'm thinking of accepting exorcism 
requests at this temple.

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:19.240
What?

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:23.610
I can't believe you showed up 
the moment I had that thought.

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:25.640
You truly are psychic.

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:27.470
Can you read minds, too?

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:29.900
No! That's not what I do...

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:32.480
I haven't received any requests yet,

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:35.200
but when I do, I'll be 
counting on you, Ashida-kun.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:36.970
It's Ashiya.

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:39.210
And you shouldn't count on me.

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:40.040
Oh, right.

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:41.330
Take a look.

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:45.460
I even made this postcard to 
hand out to my parishioners.

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:47.680
"Parishioners troubled 
by hauntings, curses,

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:49.980
and all other manner of 
supernatural phenomena,

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:51.850
we are now open for consultations.

00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:56.310
This temple is partnered 
with a talented psychic."

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:59.420
L-Look, sir, I told you...

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:01.930
I don't have any psychic abilities.

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:02.850
It's yokai that I...

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:09.000
<i>I can't even see yokai anymore.</i>

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:10.910
Don't worry.

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:13.760
I plan on paying you well.

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:15.980
Th-That's not what I'm worried about!

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:17.110
Dad.

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:19.100
<i>I'm saved from this Hell!</i>

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:21.280
<i>Although it's a priest 
that's sitting next to me.</i>

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:23.240
That's enough of that.

00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:25.640
Hanae came because he wanted to talk to me.

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:27.660
What? He has business with you?

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:30.380
<i>And now I'm back in Hell!</i>

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:31.660
Hanae, let's go.

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:33.420
Hey, wait! Masuda!

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:35.630
You'll pay if you do anything 
to hurt my daughter!

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:39.560
It's Ashiya. That's not even close anymore.

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:42.640
I'll tell Mom if you don't stop acting stupid.

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:46.240
Zenko, I'm just worried about you.

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:49.290
You don't need to worry, Dad. Just relax.

00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:51.600
Y-Yeah, that's right. Don't worry.

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:55.200
I'll have him come again
if we're hired for an exorcism.

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:56.530
R-Really?

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:03.820
Hanae, put your arm out.

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:05.300
Oh, okay.

00:10:07.030 --> 00:10:08.890
Is Yahiko there?

00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:09.480
Yeah.

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:11.530
He's behind me.

00:10:12.370 --> 00:10:14.680
Ashiya hit me with his shoe.

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:16.880
Why do I have to help him?

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:19.240
Just bite him.

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:21.000
I'll give you rakugan later.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.290
Aw, man...

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:25.160
Oh, I'll do it for ten, though.

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:25.890
Fine.

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:28.480
Really? Okay, I'll do it!

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:35.050
It's over.

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:37.100
Well? Can you see him?

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:44.990
It didn't work.

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:46.500
I see.

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:50.900
You can't see him...

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:57.010
<b>The Morose Mononokean</b>

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:03.400
Hey, Itsuki!

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:04.220
Shizuku?

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:05.930
I thought you'd already left.

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:07.600
I was just about to.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.270
So, what did you need with me?

00:11:10.630 --> 00:11:14.680
There's someone at the 
store who wants to see you.

00:11:14.680 --> 00:11:17.280
What would one of my clients 
be doing at the Kiyakudo?

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:22.420
Didn't I just tell you?

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:28.540
I brought him.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:30.340
Oh, really?

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:34.290
Abeno-dono.

00:11:35.890 --> 00:11:37.130
It's been a while.

00:11:37.540 --> 00:11:39.630
Thanks again for your help.

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:42.390
How have you been since then?

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:45.980
The pain has mostly gone,

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:47.870
thanks to this shop's medicine.

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:51.080
Yeah, of course. It's specially made.

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:55.060
Ah, I see.

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:58.640
The little ones are grateful, as well.

00:11:58.640 --> 00:11:59.850
I see.

00:12:02.710 --> 00:12:05.770
Ashiya-dono isn't with you?

00:12:05.770 --> 00:12:06.620
No.

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:09.660
That's a shame.

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:12.330
If not for you and Ashiya-dono,

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:15.330
I wouldn't be here with the little ones.

00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:21.740
I'm truly blessed to have met the two of you.

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:23.590
I owe you both my life.

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:28.100
No, I didn't save you. It was Ashiya.

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:35.770
I'm glad we caught you in time, though.

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:38.360
He came just after you left.

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:41.430
That's why I called my brother in a hurry.

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:44.270
Thanks for the help, miss.

00:12:44.270 --> 00:12:47.320
It's no problem. You're one of our regulars.

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:50.370
Oh, Shizuku, you can leave for the day.

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:51.920
Already?

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:54.990
You've been working a lot of overtime lately.

00:12:54.990 --> 00:12:57.440
I'm sure the Legislator 
will be glad to see you.

00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:58.650
Okay.

00:12:58.650 --> 00:13:00.320
See you later, Itsuki.

00:13:00.320 --> 00:13:01.840
Yeah, later.

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:04.650
Bring Ashiya with you next time.

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:06.890
If I feel like it.

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:12.110
Well?

00:13:12.110 --> 00:13:12.890
Huh?

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:15.360
This is just a hunch,

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:17.400
but did something happen to Ashiya-kun?

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:18.440
Huh?

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:20.090
You can't hide it from me.

00:13:20.090 --> 00:13:22.080
It's written all over your face.

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:23.050
Just kidding.

00:13:23.050 --> 00:13:24.090
You...

00:13:24.850 --> 00:13:27.910
That's why you suddenly sent 
Shizuku home, isn't it?

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:32.030
She doesn't even know you 
and Ashiya-kun are human.

00:13:32.030 --> 00:13:33.770
It'd be difficult to talk with her here.

00:13:36.820 --> 00:13:39.590
I didn't mean to hide it.

00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:44.800
He can't see yokai anymore?

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:47.610
Isn't there some medicine he can take?

00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:51.500
Human medicine is outside
my field of expertise...

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:55.680
It's not as though Ashiya-kun 
could always see yokai, right?

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:59.800
He began seeing them after he 
was possessed by the hairball.

00:13:59.800 --> 00:14:02.690
Before that, he couldn't see them at all.

00:14:02.990 --> 00:14:05.530
So there was a trigger.

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:10.460
Why don't you try looking for 
this Tomori-dono and talk to her?

00:14:10.460 --> 00:14:12.350
That would be ideal,

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:15.420
but if she just recently 
came to the Underworld...

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:17.820
The Legislator may know where to find her,

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:19.960
but he's so busy.

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:22.480
There's no need to go that far.

00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:26.080
Ashiya isn't my employee.

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:29.550
He has nothing to do with the 
Mononokean or yokai anymore.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:34.400
We'll go look for Tomori-dono.

00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:34.990
Huh?

00:14:34.990 --> 00:14:36.830
I've got the little ones.

00:14:36.830 --> 00:14:38.910
If we split up, we may be able to find her.

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:40.060
But...

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:44.070
Don't expect too much from us, though.

00:14:44.350 --> 00:14:47.560
I can't allow you to do this for me.

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:49.820
Like I said, I've already fired him—

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:57.130
Itsuki, you should ask them to do it.

00:14:57.560 --> 00:14:59.960
Just listen to them.

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:06.210
Then I accept your offer.

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:14.250
Abeno-dono, you wait here.

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:16.890
I wouldn't want to miss you again.

00:15:20.840 --> 00:15:23.900
They love Ashiya-kun, too.

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:24.730
Huh?

00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:28.780
I love him, too.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:30.110
He's adorable.

00:15:35.430 --> 00:15:39.160
She was recently exorcised by the Mononokean.

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:40.620
The Mononokean?

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:52.480
You know her?

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:55.950
Indeed. I know her very well.

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:59.610
Like myself, she recently 
came from the Mundane World.

00:15:59.610 --> 00:16:02.330
We found that we had much to talk about.

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:04.400
Anyway, why are you looking for Tomori-san?

00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:09.900
Standing there won't do any good.

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:13.410
What's wrong?

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:16.570
My job is to help yokai.

00:16:17.190 --> 00:16:20.590
Asking yokai to help me is pathetic.

00:16:20.590 --> 00:16:22.160
You're wrong.

00:16:23.350 --> 00:16:26.260
That is how it works, yes,

00:16:26.740 --> 00:16:29.020
but they're the ones who asked to help.

00:16:29.640 --> 00:16:33.050
Because they wanted to help Ashiya-kun.

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:36.700
I fired him already.

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:39.060
Even if I meet Tomori-dono now...

00:16:39.340 --> 00:16:44.400
But don't you think it's incredible 
that yokai are doing their best

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:46.060
to help a human?

00:16:56.220 --> 00:17:00.320
Itsuki, does this mean they 
found her, or they didn't?

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:01.780
Don't ask me!

00:17:04.720 --> 00:17:06.840
Quiet, little ones.

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:08.840
Abeno-dono.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:13.840
We know where she is.

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:16.720
Long time, no see.

00:17:17.070 --> 00:17:18.010
Nobou-dono.

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:20.720
They explained the situation to me.

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:23.930
Upon learning that Ashiya-dono is in trouble,

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:26.730
I couldn't just sit still, so here I am.

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:31.260
Hey! What's wrong with that Ashiya kid?

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:35.240
Is it true that Ashiya can no longer see us?

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:36.990
Y-Yes.

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:38.780
This is serious.

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:41.180
It's because Ashiya could see us

00:17:41.180 --> 00:17:44.790
that I'm able to fly with the princess now.

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:46.520
Princess!

00:17:49.240 --> 00:17:50.310
Why?

00:17:50.820 --> 00:17:54.150
I previously told you that 
Ashiya-sama was dangerous.

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:56.260
Mitsuchigura-dono.

00:17:56.640 --> 00:18:00.100
My fears may have been baseless.

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:01.760
After all,

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:06.770
we're all here because 
we're worried about him.

00:18:09.970 --> 00:18:13.510
He's so well-liked by yokai, 
even though he's human.

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:16.550
Reminds me of someone else I know.

00:18:19.920 --> 00:18:21.700
I'm going to see Tomori-dono.

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:29.040
Oh, you're...

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:34.550
I'm sorry for coming by 
unannounced, Tomori-dono.

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:39.070
His eyes?

00:18:39.070 --> 00:18:42.410
Yes. They still haven't recovered.

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:45.060
I thought I should come talk to you.

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:48.440
In the past, those who lent me their vision

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:51.080
had it restored after two or three days.

00:18:51.080 --> 00:18:54.360
Yes, that's what Okina-dono told us.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:56.060
Otherwise,

00:18:56.060 --> 00:19:00.620
I never would have accepted 
Ashiya-dono's offer.

00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:01.700
But...

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:03.580
Tomori-dono?

00:19:03.920 --> 00:19:06.100
There may be some other reason

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:09.580
it's taking so long to return.

00:19:09.930 --> 00:19:11.710
What kind of reason?

00:19:12.640 --> 00:19:17.860
I can tell he feels strongly about our kind.

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:24.480
His desire to grant me 
his vision was so strong,

00:19:24.480 --> 00:19:29.100
it's possible that it still 
subconsciously remains.

00:19:29.720 --> 00:19:31.840
<i>That's definitely possible.</i>

00:19:31.840 --> 00:19:37.520
However, if his condition persists much longer,

00:19:37.520 --> 00:19:42.020
Ashiya-dono may permanently lose his ability.

00:19:43.480 --> 00:19:45.910
I'm worried he might.

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:48.220
Indeed...

00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:53.400
Ashiya hasn't always been able to see yokai.

00:19:53.940 --> 00:19:56.130
What you've described may be possible.

00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:58.120
I'm so sorry.

00:19:58.120 --> 00:20:01.610
This is the result of my own selfishness,

00:20:02.020 --> 00:20:05.020
because I presumed on Ashiya-dono's kindness.

00:20:05.520 --> 00:20:07.210
If I could,

00:20:07.210 --> 00:20:11.140
I would give my eyes to him.

00:20:11.720 --> 00:20:12.650
No need.

00:20:14.840 --> 00:20:17.520
You have nothing to worry about.

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:19.130
Abeno-dono...

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:22.970
I'm responsible as well, for not stopping him.

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:24.730
But...

00:20:25.480 --> 00:20:27.240
Please don't worry.

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:29.870
I'll make sure he learns to see again,

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:33.080
so you don't have to suffer anymore.

00:20:35.080 --> 00:20:39.130
Besides, it seems the 
Mononokean still needs him.

00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:44.580
<i>I know what I told her...</i>

00:20:46.150 --> 00:20:48.220
<i>But what am I supposed to do?</i>

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:51.610
Mononokean, come.

00:20:56.880 --> 00:20:59.450
<i>A malady of the mind, huh?</i>

00:21:07.670 --> 00:21:09.080
Sorry, Ashiya.

00:21:09.840 --> 00:21:11.880
I can't go back yet.

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:15.200
Sorry for coming over so late.

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:16.120
It's fine.

00:21:16.630 --> 00:21:18.460
Abeno still isn't back at school?

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:21.920
No. Seems like it must be a pretty big job.

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:24.710
Not that it's any of my business.

00:21:25.690 --> 00:21:28.720
There must be a way for you to see again.

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:30.970
You might suddenly be able to see tomorrow.

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:33.270
Yeah. Thanks, Zenko.

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:34.480
Bye.

00:21:36.580 --> 00:21:38.980
Why didn't you tell him?

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:39.730
Shh.

00:21:40.340 --> 00:21:43.580
Hmph. Ashiya can't hear me anyway.

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:48.990
After all, he can't even see that.

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Next Time "The End"</b>

00:23:25.810 --> 00:23:26.730
Abeno-san!

00:23:26.730 --> 00:23:27.390
Huh?

00:23:27.390 --> 00:23:30.300
I know we've been through a lot.

00:23:30.300 --> 00:23:33.530
Just so, so, so much...

00:23:33.530 --> 00:23:34.640
What are you trying to say?

00:23:34.640 --> 00:23:38.080
But I hope you'll continue to 
help me with all kinds of things!

00:23:38.080 --> 00:23:39.750
You were annoying to the end!
